(2) The integration of programs and activities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be incorporated into planning and budget documents which include:
   a. regional long-term development plan;
   b. regional medium-term development plan;
   c. strategic plan of Regional Apparatus;
   d. work plan of Regional Government; and
   e. work plan and budget of Regional Apparatus.
(3) The Regional Apparatus handling the field of Women shall facilitate the integration of policies, programs, and activities for the Protection of Women into the preparation of planning and budget documents as referred to in paragraph (2).
(4) In carrying out activities as referred to in paragraph (3), the Regional Apparatus handling the field of Women shall coordinate with Regional Apparatus that have direct relevance to the field of Women.

